    == PHASE 12 — Flows reference catalogs first-class (Phase 7.4.2) ==

    The most important new mechanic: a flow's incoming is canonically a
    catalog row (NOT an edge id). This phase exercises declaration,
    fan-out, both read tools, the new contract on get_flow_inverse,
    and the negative-path validation.

    12a. DECLARE A FLOW (single):
         sme-monolith owns a catalog "POST /payments/charge" (declared
         in Phase 2) and a bound outgoing edge to feeds-db at
         "INSERT ledger" (declared in Phase 3 or freshly here via
         upsert_edge_outbound). Wire them:
           upsert_flow(
             agent_id=sme-monolith,
             component_id=monolith_component_id,
             incoming_catalog_id=<POST /payments/charge catalog id>,
             outgoing_edge_id=<INSERT ledger edge id>,
             metadata={"src": "code"}, confidence=0.9,
           )
         Verify the returned row has incoming_catalog_id set (NOT
         incoming_edge_id — that column does not exist anymore).

    12b. FAN-OUT (one catalog → multiple outgoings):
         Add a SECOND outgoing from monolith — e.g. a publishes_to
         to a notify topic — and wire a second flow:
           upsert_flow(monolith, monolith_id, charge_catalog_id,
                       <notify edge id>)
         Confirm get_flow(monolith_id, charge_catalog_id) returns
         BOTH outgoings (set-based fan-out).

    12c. INVERSE LOOKUP (contract change verification):
         get_flow_inverse(monolith_id, <INSERT ledger edge id>) should
         return CATALOG ROWS (not edge rows). Verify the returned row
         has a `kind` field (catalog rows do; edge rows don't) and
         that its id matches charge_catalog_id.

    12d. NEGATIVE PATH — foreign-component catalog refused:
         sme-monolith tries to upsert_flow using sme-cron's catalog id
         as incoming_catalog_id (a catalog NOT belonging to monolith's
         component). Should raise ValueError matching
         "does not belong to component".

    12e. CATALOG CASCADE — flow disappears when catalog is deleted:
